# Copy to `forbidden.local.txt` (which git ignores) and fill in the strings
# that must never appear in a publishable file: your name, handles, email
# addresses, private paths, and any personal disclosure you do not want in a
# shared repository.
#
# One pattern per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. Matching is
# a case-insensitive literal substring test, so `Smith` also catches `smith`.
#
# A line starting with `!` is an exemption: a repo-relative path glob whose
# hits are expected and should not fail the gate. Use it for files that must
# record a real name to stay correct — machine inventory naming a Unix account,
# for instance — rather than weakening the patterns themselves.
#
# `bin/check --scan` reads this file and fails on any hit across the tracked and
# untracked-but-not-ignored files of every scanned repository. If the file is
# absent the identity scan is skipped, which is the intended behavior for a
# fresh clone by someone other than the original author.

# Ada Lovelace
# alovelace
# ada@example.com
# ~/library/ada
